    "q-37248": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37248",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Consider a rule between $x$ and $y$ given by the table below.\n\n| **$x$** | $12$ | $9$ | $7$ | $3$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $15$ | $12$ | $9$ | $6$ | $3$ | $0$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The rule is a function\n\nII. The rule is **not** a function\n\nIII. The rule maps the input $x=15$ to the output $y=12$",
      "worked_solution": "A rule is a function if and only if every input is mapped to precisely one output.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false, and statement II is true. \n\n| **$x$** | $12$ | $9$ | $7$ | $3$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $15$ | $12$ | $9$ | $6$ | $3$ | $0$ |\n\nNotice that the first row contains the value $x=9$ twice. The input value $x=9$ is assigned to *more than one* output value ($12$ and $0$).\n\n- Statement III is false. The input $x=15$ is not mapped to anything.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
